1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,496
In this lesson,

2
00:00:01,496 --> 00:00:03,421
you build CloudCart yourself.

3
00:00:03,421 --> 00:00:04,218
One command,

4
00:00:04,218 --> 00:00:07,073
and Maven turns source code into a web app,

5
00:00:07,073 --> 00:00:08,201
ready for Tomcat.

6
00:00:08,751 --> 00:00:12,485
Today is lesson two: the project layout, and the Maven build.

7
00:00:13,035 --> 00:00:14,512
You will read the project,

8
00:00:14,512 --> 00:00:15,308
run the build,

9
00:00:15,308 --> 00:00:16,615
open the finished file,

10
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:19,456
and answer four questions about what is inside it.

11
00:00:20,006 --> 00:00:22,886
Last lesson, you used the app. Today, you make it.

12
00:00:24,436 --> 00:00:27,508
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

13
00:00:28,058 --> 00:00:32,837
One: look. The folders of a real Java web project, and what lives in each.

14
00:00:33,387 --> 00:00:38,635
Two: read. The pom.xml, the one file that tells Maven everything.

15
00:00:39,185 --> 00:00:43,878
Three: build. Test first, then package, and watch every step Maven takes.

16
00:00:44,428 --> 00:00:48,396
Four: open. Look inside the finished war file, without Tomcat.

17
00:00:48,946 --> 00:00:53,383
Five: your turn. Change the version, build again, and a lab checks your work.

18
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:58,776
And the lessons ahead: deploy it, run it and fix it, then prove it from a clean copy.

19
00:00:59,326 --> 00:01:00,841
Look, read, build, open.

20
00:01:02,891 --> 00:01:05,771
Before the terminal, one idea. What is Maven?

21
00:01:06,321 --> 00:01:12,252
Maven is a build tool. You describe the project in one file, the pom. Maven does the rest.

22
00:01:12,802 --> 00:01:15,818
It downloads the libraries your project needs,

23
00:01:15,818 --> 00:01:17,064
from Maven Central.

24
00:01:17,064 --> 00:01:18,901
That is a huge public store,

25
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:19,884
and it is free.

26
00:01:20,434 --> 00:01:23,593
Then it follows a fixed lifecycle: compile your code,

27
00:01:23,593 --> 00:01:24,470
run your tests,

28
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:25,640
and pack the result.

29
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:27,383
If one step fails,

30
00:01:27,383 --> 00:01:28,178
Maven stops.

31
00:01:28,178 --> 00:01:31,028
A broken build never reaches the next step,

32
00:01:31,028 --> 00:01:33,016
and it never reaches a server.

33
00:01:33,566 --> 00:01:38,260
Pom, Central, lifecycle. Keep these three words. We use them in every lesson.

34
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:45,954
Go to the project. Type: cd /opt/lab114/cloudcart

35
00:01:47,084 --> 00:01:49,431
Look at the top level. Type: ls

36
00:01:49,561 --> 00:01:51,422
Only three things: a README,

37
00:01:51,422 --> 00:01:52,578
the pom.xml,

38
00:01:52,578 --> 00:01:53,990
and the source folder.

39
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:55,017
Everything else,

40
00:01:55,017 --> 00:01:56,494
the build makes for us.

41
00:01:57,044 --> 00:02:05,193
Now the main code. Type: find src/main -type f | sort | cut -c10-

42
00:02:05,323 --> 00:02:06,381
Three folders.

43
00:02:06,381 --> 00:02:07,891
Java holds the code.

44
00:02:07,891 --> 00:02:10,157
It sits in a package: academy,

45
00:02:10,157 --> 00:02:11,366
then CloudCart.

46
00:02:11,366 --> 00:02:12,272
Eight files,

47
00:02:12,272 --> 00:02:14,311
one for each job: products,

48
00:02:14,311 --> 00:02:14,991
the cart,

49
00:02:14,991 --> 00:02:15,595
pricing,

50
00:02:15,595 --> 00:02:16,124
orders,

51
00:02:16,124 --> 00:02:16,577
users,

52
00:02:16,577 --> 00:02:17,483
and the API.

53
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:22,407
Resources holds a file the app reads while it runs. Here, its version.

54
00:02:22,957 --> 00:02:27,206
And web app holds everything the browser gets: the pages,

55
00:02:27,206 --> 00:02:27,951
the style,

56
00:02:27,951 --> 00:02:28,846
the scripts.

57
00:02:28,846 --> 00:02:29,591
Inside it,

58
00:02:29,591 --> 00:02:31,679
the WEB-INF folder,

59
00:02:31,679 --> 00:02:33,095
with web.xml.

60
00:02:33,095 --> 00:02:36,226
That file tells Tomcat how to run the app.

61
00:02:36,776 --> 00:02:41,427
And the tests. Type: find src/test -type f

62
00:02:41,557 --> 00:02:42,663
Four test files,

63
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,736
with thirty-two tests in them.

64
00:02:44,736 --> 00:02:45,980
They check prices,

65
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:46,395
stock,

66
00:02:46,395 --> 00:02:46,879
orders,

67
00:02:46,879 --> 00:02:47,708
and the API.

68
00:02:47,708 --> 00:02:50,197
Maven runs them every time we build.

69
00:02:50,747 --> 00:02:58,427
Now the heart of it: the pom. First, its name. Type: sed -n 5,9p pom.xml

70
00:02:58,557 --> 00:03:01,929
Three words give a project its address: group,

71
00:03:01,929 --> 00:03:02,589
artifact,

72
00:03:02,589 --> 00:03:03,469
and version.

73
00:03:03,469 --> 00:03:05,669
Group: academy.cloudcart.

74
00:03:05,669 --> 00:03:07,208
Artifact: CloudCart.

75
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:09,628
Version: 0.2.0.

76
00:03:09,628 --> 00:03:11,314
And the packaging: war.

77
00:03:11,864 --> 00:03:18,285
Then the libraries. Type: sed -n 15,27p pom.xml

78
00:03:18,415 --> 00:03:19,803
Three dependencies.

79
00:03:19,803 --> 00:03:21,336
Jakarta servlet API,

80
00:03:21,336 --> 00:03:22,431
scope provided.

81
00:03:22,431 --> 00:03:24,694
That means: Tomcat supplies it,

82
00:03:24,694 --> 00:03:26,885
so we only need it to compile.

83
00:03:27,435 --> 00:03:27,873
Gson,

84
00:03:27,873 --> 00:03:29,335
the J S O N library,

85
00:03:29,335 --> 00:03:30,358
with no scope.

86
00:03:30,358 --> 00:03:32,257
It is packed into the app.

87
00:03:32,257 --> 00:03:33,061
And JUnit,

88
00:03:33,061 --> 00:03:35,692
scope test: only used while testing,

89
00:03:35,692 --> 00:03:36,715
never shipped.

90
00:03:37,265 --> 00:03:38,385
Now we build.

91
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:38,902
First,

92
00:03:38,902 --> 00:03:40,711
only up to the tests.

93
00:03:40,711 --> 00:03:42,263
Type: mvn -B test,

94
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:46,054
then a filter to keep the lines that matter.

95
00:03:58,604 --> 00:03:59,764
Watch the steps,

96
00:03:59,764 --> 00:04:00,417
in order.

97
00:04:00,417 --> 00:04:01,142
Resources.

98
00:04:01,142 --> 00:04:01,722
Compile.

99
00:04:01,722 --> 00:04:02,809
Test resources.

100
00:04:02,809 --> 00:04:03,752
Test compile.

101
00:04:03,752 --> 00:04:06,724
Then surefire runs the tests: thirty-two,

102
00:04:06,724 --> 00:04:07,594
no failures.

103
00:04:07,594 --> 00:04:08,609
Build success.

104
00:04:09,159 --> 00:04:13,142
Maven downloaded every library it needed from Maven Central,

105
00:04:13,142 --> 00:04:14,336
on this first run.

106
00:04:14,336 --> 00:04:14,999
Next time,

107
00:04:14,999 --> 00:04:16,925
they come from a local cache.

108
00:04:17,475 --> 00:04:20,568
Did it make the web app yet? Type: ls target

109
00:04:20,698 --> 00:04:21,219
Classes,

110
00:04:21,219 --> 00:04:22,066
test classes,

111
00:04:22,066 --> 00:04:23,433
and the test reports.

112
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:24,475
But no war file.

113
00:04:24,475 --> 00:04:26,885
The test step stops before packaging.

114
00:04:27,435 --> 00:04:32,811
Now the whole lifecycle. Type: mvn -B package, with the same filter.

115
00:04:45,761 --> 00:04:46,717
The same steps,

116
00:04:46,717 --> 00:04:49,332
and one more at the end: the war plugin.

117
00:04:49,332 --> 00:04:50,161
Building war,

118
00:04:50,161 --> 00:04:50,799
in target.

119
00:04:50,799 --> 00:04:51,691
Build success.

120
00:04:52,241 --> 00:04:57,212
How big is it? Type: ls -lh target/cloudcart.war

121
00:04:57,342 --> 00:05:01,865
About three hundred kilobytes. One small file, with the whole app inside it.

122
00:05:02,415 --> 00:05:03,377
Open it,

123
00:05:03,377 --> 00:05:05,181
without Tomcat.

124
00:05:05,181 --> 00:05:08,187
A war file is a zip file.

125
00:05:08,187 --> 00:05:12,637
Type: unzip -Z1 target/cloudcart.war,

126
00:05:12,637 --> 00:05:14,681
then two filters.

127
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:16,901
The inside of the war.

128
00:05:16,901 --> 00:05:17,660
The pages,

129
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:18,419
the style,

130
00:05:18,419 --> 00:05:19,330
the scripts.

131
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:22,139
Then WEB-INF: web.xml,

132
00:05:22,139 --> 00:05:23,429
the version file,

133
00:05:23,429 --> 00:05:25,175
and one library: Gson.

134
00:05:25,175 --> 00:05:26,845
That is the whole app,

135
00:05:26,845 --> 00:05:28,970
except the compiled classes.

136
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:37,669
And the compiled classes. Type: unzip -Z1 target/cloudcart.war | grep -c '.class$'

137
00:05:37,799 --> 00:05:39,342
Fifteen compiled classes,

138
00:05:39,342 --> 00:05:41,069
from the eight source files.

139
00:05:41,069 --> 00:05:42,920
Some files hold inner classes,

140
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,202
so there are more classes than files.

141
00:05:45,752 --> 00:05:48,306
Remember the version file?

142
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:55,181
Type: unzip -p target/cloudcart.war WEB-INF/classes/version.properties

143
00:05:55,311 --> 00:05:56,228
In the source,

144
00:05:56,228 --> 00:05:57,603
it said: dollar sign,

145
00:05:57,603 --> 00:05:58,651
project version.

146
00:05:58,651 --> 00:06:01,270
Maven replaced it with the real version,

147
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:02,514
and the build time.

148
00:06:02,514 --> 00:06:04,151
This is called filtering.

149
00:06:04,151 --> 00:06:06,639
Remember this time: it is in your lab.

150
00:06:07,189 --> 00:06:14,229
And the servlet API library? Type: unzip -Z1 target/cloudcart.war | grep -c servlet

151
00:06:14,359 --> 00:06:18,413
Zero. Provided means: not in the war. Tomcat already has it.

152
00:06:18,963 --> 00:06:28,115
Now change the version. Type: sed -i to replace 0.2.0 with 0.2.1 in pom.xml

153
00:06:28,245 --> 00:06:35,669
Build again, from a clean start. Type: mvn -B -q clean package. The -q means quiet.

154
00:06:45,219 --> 00:06:47,786
Clean deleted the target folder first.

155
00:06:47,786 --> 00:06:50,218
Then the whole lifecycle ran again.

156
00:06:50,218 --> 00:06:52,515
Quiet means: no news is good news.

157
00:06:53,065 --> 00:06:57,715
Check the war. Type: unzip -p target/cloudcart.war WEB-INF/classes/version.properties

158
00:07:00,445 --> 00:07:01,998
Zero point two point one,

159
00:07:01,998 --> 00:07:03,302
and a new build time.

160
00:07:03,302 --> 00:07:04,543
One line in the pom,

161
00:07:04,543 --> 00:07:06,158
and the whole app changed.

162
00:07:06,158 --> 00:07:07,275
That is your task,

163
00:07:07,275 --> 00:07:08,083
in miniature.

164
00:07:09,633 --> 00:07:13,409
Your task. Build CloudCart, and prove what is inside the war.

165
00:07:13,959 --> 00:07:16,391
One: lab up. It gives you the real source.

166
00:07:16,941 --> 00:07:20,973
Two: build it as it is, with mvn package, and read the summary.

167
00:07:21,523 --> 00:07:26,515
Three: edit the pom with vim. Version 0.2.1. Build again.

168
00:07:27,065 --> 00:07:29,161
Four: open the war with unzip.

169
00:07:29,161 --> 00:07:31,054
Then write answers.txt,

170
00:07:31,054 --> 00:07:32,541
four lines: the tests,

171
00:07:32,541 --> 00:07:33,353
the library,

172
00:07:33,353 --> 00:07:34,975
the provided dependency,

173
00:07:34,975 --> 00:07:36,260
and the build time.

174
00:07:36,810 --> 00:07:39,860
Five: lab check. Five checks. Then lab down.

175
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:46,113
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

176
00:07:46,663 --> 00:07:48,311
The lab lives on GitHub,

177
00:07:48,311 --> 00:07:49,478
at it-waves,

178
00:07:49,478 --> 00:07:51,057
/devops-ai,

179
00:07:51,057 --> 00:07:52,568
in the folder academy,

180
00:07:52,568 --> 00:07:53,255
/lab.

181
00:07:53,805 --> 00:07:59,309
Two files: lab114.sh, and shortcuts114.sh.

182
00:07:59,859 --> 00:08:00,771
Install it,

183
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:03,673
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

184
00:08:03,673 --> 00:08:05,581
-m 755,

185
00:08:05,581 --> 00:08:07,654
lab114.sh,

186
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:08,898
into /usr

187
00:08:08,898 --> 00:08:09,893
/local

188
00:08:09,893 --> 00:08:10,888
/sbin.

189
00:08:11,438 --> 00:08:16,558
Load the short name with: source shortcuts114.sh. You get: lab.

190
00:08:17,108 --> 00:08:18,314
You need a JDK,

191
00:08:18,314 --> 00:08:18,740
Maven,

192
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:19,095
curl,

193
00:08:19,095 --> 00:08:19,804
and unzip,

194
00:08:19,804 --> 00:08:21,862
about one gigabyte of memory,

195
00:08:21,862 --> 00:08:22,784
and internet,

196
00:08:22,784 --> 00:08:24,061
for Maven Central.

197
00:08:24,061 --> 00:08:26,687
The lab downloads the source for you.

198
00:08:27,237 --> 00:08:32,698
Lab check judges your work. Lab down removes everything. Only run it on your own machine.

199
00:08:34,748 --> 00:08:36,817
Pass or fail. You need all five.

200
00:08:37,367 --> 00:08:39,565
The war exists, and it is a valid zip.

201
00:08:40,115 --> 00:08:43,720
The pom, and the war, both say 0.2.1.

202
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,553
Your test count is the one Maven ran.

203
00:08:47,103 --> 00:08:50,345
Your library, and your provided dependency, are right.

204
00:08:50,895 --> 00:08:54,245
Your build time comes from inside the war, not from the clock.

205
00:08:54,795 --> 00:08:56,096
To pass, all five.

206
00:08:58,146 --> 00:08:59,917
Your turn, on your own machine.

207
00:09:00,467 --> 00:09:02,536
One: lab up, and read the task list.

208
00:09:03,086 --> 00:09:05,326
Two: look at the layout, and build once.

209
00:09:05,876 --> 00:09:10,377
Three: set version 0.2.1 with vim, and build again.

210
00:09:10,927 --> 00:09:13,615
Four: open the war, and write the four answers.

211
00:09:14,165 --> 00:09:17,152
Five: lab check, until you see five out of five.

212
00:09:17,702 --> 00:09:19,046
Six: lab down.

213
00:09:19,596 --> 00:09:21,431
Pause the video, and begin now.

214
00:09:36,981 --> 00:09:37,856
Quick check.

215
00:09:38,406 --> 00:09:41,392
Which file tells Maven everything about the project?

216
00:09:41,942 --> 00:09:44,737
Why is the servlet API not inside the war?

217
00:09:45,287 --> 00:09:47,122
What did the test step stop before?

218
00:09:47,672 --> 00:09:50,274
Where did the build time inside the war come from?

219
00:09:50,824 --> 00:09:53,820
Objective covered: CloudCart version zero,

220
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:56,601
the project layout and the Maven build.

221
00:09:56,601 --> 00:09:56,958
Look,

222
00:09:56,958 --> 00:09:57,314
read,

223
00:09:57,314 --> 00:09:57,742
build,

224
00:09:57,742 --> 00:09:58,099
open.

225
00:09:58,649 --> 00:10:00,718
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

226
00:10:11,268 --> 00:10:14,895
Next: deploy it to Tomcat, by hand, and from the Manager.

227
00:10:15,445 --> 00:10:18,773
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
